# r1os: the R1's side button is the power key on mtk-kpd (scancode 116). BUTTON_1 stops it from
# turning the screen off; WAKE keeps a press waking the screen. r1d reads the button straight from
# evdev and owns tap / double-tap / hold (double-tap on home turns the screen off). The PMIC's
# hardware long-press power-off is unaffected. (Remap from r1ptt / ClawPTT; see NOTICE.md.)
key 116   BUTTON_1      WAKE
key 114   VOLUME_DOWN
